  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_FACTOR_PASS, but this is the strongest new-information-domain near-miss in the current post-protocol search. F-MARGIN-LEV-US raised full-history CAGR to 14.440021% versus V11 14.345615% and improved Sharpe versus its matched unconditional retention control (1.516685 versus 1.493322), while keeping MDD at 8.612794%. However full Sharpe remained slightly below V11 1.522263 and the candidate beat the matched control in only 3/7 fixed folds. Paired 63-session moving-block bootstrap over 20,000 replicates gave P(CAGR candidate > V11)=81.730% and P(Sharpe candidate > matched)=85.365%, below the frozen 90% gates; both median incremental deltas were positive and candidate MDD P97.5=14.292% passed the 15% risk gate. Cumulative 27-trial DSR probability was 93.455%, below the frozen 95% requirement. Per the stop rule, no denominator, normalization, lookback, threshold, sign, retention, stale-rule or publication-lag rescue is permitted. Because the evidence is suggestive but not robust-certified, the only allowed continuation is a separately preregistered prospective shadow from a new freeze date, without modifying this historical rule.",
